display_name="Fygo Cinema"
desc="Fygo TV on your TV: the Fygo TV (飞牛影视) library and player fullscreen on a TV connected to the NAS, driven by a remote, with hardware video decoding. It signs in by itself with the account you enter, starts when the TV is plugged in and plays through the TV's speakers. Requires Appliance Compositor and Fygo TV."
changelog="1.1.1: after a reboot the TV no longer stays black with a thin line and an unresponsive remote (the TV app started before Fygo TV was ready and kept its error page); it now shows “Connecting to Fygo TV…” and goes on by itself as soon as Fygo TV is up. The focus ring also comes back by itself if a page loads without one. 1.1.0: the remote stays with the TV while Fygo Cinema runs, also when the front panel's screen goes dark (needs Appliance Compositor 1.1). Moving the TV to another port, or choosing another TV screen on the admin page, no longer restarts the display server, so the other screens are not interrupted (with Appliance Compositor 1.1; older ones are still restarted). While the TV is unplugged its window never shows on another screen. Unplugging the TV now stops the TV app cleanly. 1.0.0: first release. Fygo TV fullscreen on the TV, driven by a remote: arrow-key navigation with a focus ring on every page, OK and Back; in the player, up/down bring up the controls (speed, quality, subtitles, audio track). Hardware video decoding up to 4K HDR. Signs in by itself with the account entered on the admin page and stays signed in across restarts; without an account, or when sign-in fails, the TV shows what to do with a QR code instead of a black screen. Starts when the TV is plugged in and stops when it is unplugged; plays through the TV's speakers; the remote's volume keys set the TV volume with an on-screen display. The page is sized for the screen (200 % above 1080p, 150 % otherwise, adjustable). Admin and account controls are hidden from the remote."

